        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4427,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1953,
        "paragraph_id": "323391EA",
        "text": "In (C.21) zaquifer is the level of the bottom of the aquifer. As described in Section 3.3.6, the head applied on the top boundary of the groundwater domain (Hbc) depends on whether the groundwater and surface water are connected or unconnected:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 91515,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4431,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1957,
        "paragraph_id": "4DCC9109",
        "text": "In (C.22) the parameter κr is the relative numerical ‘connectedness’ of the groundwater and surface water head, determined by linear interpolation across the numerical smoothing constant ε."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 91589,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4433,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1959,
        "paragraph_id": "58ACAA5E",
        "text": "In the case of hydrostatic groundwater flow, the groundwater head in each cell is set equal to the head applied on the top boundary of the groundwater domain (Hbc) and the horizontal groundwater flux is computed from the groundwater head gradient:"
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
